  "fields": [
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-1-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The voice from heaven at the Jordan joins Psalm 2 and Isaiah 42: Thou art my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased. First principle: the baptism is a coronation — the anointed Son presented by the Father's own word.",
      "density": 2.3964,
      "words": 41,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-2-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The Sabbath was made for man, and not man for the sabbath: therefore the Son of man is Lord also of it. First principle: the rest-day is a gift from creation week, and its Lord was there when it was made.",
      "density": 2.2821,
      "words": 41,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-12-29",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Asked for the first commandment, Jesus recites the Shema. First principle: undivided love for the one God — heart, soul, mind, strength — is the summary of all law, fulfilled in Christ's own devotion.",
      "density": 2.2786,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 25,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-1-15",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Jesus preaches: The time is fulfilled, and the kingdom of God is at hand. First principle: Daniel's clock has run out — prophecy is not merely written, it has arrived, and the answer is repent and believe.",
      "density": 2.2393,
      "words": 37,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-13-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The Son of man appears as Daniel 7 saw Him — in the clouds with power and great glory, gathering His elect. First principle: the second coming is Daniel 7 with the sky torn open.",
      "density": 2.1321,
      "words": 35,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-1-3",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Isaiah 40:3 is John's job description in the wilderness. First principle: the way prepared is the way of the LORD Himself — John baptizes the God whose road he levels.",
      "density": 1.95,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Isaiah 40:3"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-15-34",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The ninth-hour cry opens Psalm 22 on the cross. First principle: the forsakenness is real and foretold — the righteous Sufferer bears abandonment so the forsaken need never be alone.",
      "density": 1.95,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-9-12",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Jesus holds two Scriptures together: Elijah restores first, and the Son of man suffers and is set at nought. First principle: glory and suffering are both written; the disciples kept only the glory part.",
      "density": 1.9357,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-13-14",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Jesus points readers back to Daniel for the standing desecration in the holy place — then commands flight. First principle: Daniel 8–12 is Jesus' own reference library for the end; read it before you need it.",
      "density": 1.9286,
      "words": 36,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-7-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Jesus applies Isaiah 29 to the tradition-keepers: lips near, heart far. First principle: worship by ordinance while the heart is absent is the prophecy of vain religion, fulfilled in every generation.",
      "density": 1.9179,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-14-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "On the way to Gethsemane Jesus quotes Zechariah 13:7 — smite the shepherd, and the sheep scatter. First principle: even the disciples' panic was in the script; the smitten Shepherd is the LORD's own Fellow.",
      "density": 1.9036,
      "words": 35,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Zechariah 13:7"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-1-2",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Mark opens his gospel by quoting the promise of the messenger — Behold, I send my messenger before thy face. First principle: the good news begins with a prophecy kept.",
      "density": 1.8929,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-7-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Tradition that voids the fifth commandment meets the written law. First principle: the Word of God stands over custom — honour and care for parents is not negotiable by corban.",
      "density": 1.8929,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-12-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Psalm 118's rejected Stone is quoted in the temple courts. First principle: the leaders holding the building reject the cornerstone — and God builds on the Stone they refuse.",
      "density": 1.8107,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-2-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The scribes ask the right question about the wrong Man. First principle: the forgiveness Christ speaks is a divine prerogative — the healing proves the authority is real.",
      "density": 1.7286,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "mrk-12-36",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Psalm 110 is David's Spirit-inspired words about his Lord enthroned till enemies become a footstool. First principle: the Spirit authored prophecy — and it names David's Son as David's Lord.",
